    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-dehydration-balance","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-dehydration","anchor":{"section":"What is dehydration?"},"note":"MedlinePlus defines dehydration as losing more fluid than is taken in. It establishes neither dehydration nor fluid amount for a particular actor.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-dehydration-symptoms","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-dehydration","anchor":{"section":"What are the symptoms of dehydration?"},"note":"The page lists possible adult symptoms including thirst, dry mouth, reduced urination or sweating, dark urine, tiredness and dizziness. It does not diagnose an individual from any sign.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-dehydration-assessment","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-dehydration","anchor":{"section":"How is dehydration diagnosed?"},"note":"The page describes physical examination, vital signs and symptom history, with possible blood and urine tests. It does not authorize a game claim to be treated as a medical diagnosis.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-burn-causes","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-burns","anchor":{"section":"Summary"},"note":"The page identifies tissue damage from heat, chemicals, electricity, sunlight or radiation as burns. It establishes no particular exposure or injury.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-burn-barrier","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-burns","anchor":{"section":"Summary"},"note":"The page says burns can lead to infection because they damage the skin protective barrier. It establishes no wound infection, severity or treatment.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-burn-severity","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-medlineplus-burns","anchor":{"section":"Summary"},"note":"The page states that treatment depends on cause, depth and body area covered. It establishes no treatment or outcome for a particular burn.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-foodborne-symptoms","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-cdc-food-symptoms","anchor":{"section":"Common symptoms"},"note":"CDC lists upset stomach, cramps, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea and fever as common food-poisoning symptoms. It establishes neither cause nor diagnosis for a particular illness.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-moon-phases","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-nasa-moon-phases","anchor":{"section":"Moon phases"},"note":"NASA explains that the apparent illuminated portion of the Moon changes through lunar phases. It establishes no date, sky position, weather, illumination value or navigation result.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-fda-cross-contact","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-fda-safe-food-handling","anchor":{"section":"Separate"},"note":"FDA safe-food guidance separates raw meat, poultry, seafood and eggs from other foods to avoid cross-contamination. It establishes no contamination event or illness.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-fda-clean","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-fda-safe-food-handling","anchor":{"section":"Clean"},"note":"FDA safe-food guidance includes cleaning hands and food-contact surfaces. It establishes no present cleanliness or microbial state.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:candidate-v6-usda-raw-meat","source_ref":"source:candidate-v6-usda-meat-catfish","anchor":{"section":"Safe handling"},"note":"USDA FSIS safe-handling guidance treats raw meat and catfish as food-safety handling contexts. It establishes no individual food condition or contamination.","review_status":"approved"}
